WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.258
- Peter Piper picked a peck--

00:00:01.258 --> 00:00:02.175
- Peck of pickled peppers.

00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:03.231
- Picked it? Or packed a pick?

00:00:03.231 --> 00:00:04.440
- Picked a peck.

00:00:08.002 --> 00:00:10.778
- Pickles make me think
of family, fun, summer.

00:00:10.778 --> 00:00:12.298
- I feel like I'm a pickle novice.

00:00:12.298 --> 00:00:13.612
- I don't eat pickles very often.

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:15.632
So this is going to be an adventure.

00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:17.047
- [Voiceover] Pickled eggs.

00:00:17.047 --> 00:00:17.827
Well, I actually thought that

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:19.488
these only existed in cartoons.

00:00:19.488 --> 00:00:21.642
- It's kind of like a bouncy ball.

00:00:21.642 --> 00:00:23.169
- Oh, hm mm.

00:00:23.479 --> 00:00:24.620
- Very sour.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:26.002
- This is sour.

00:00:26.002 --> 00:00:26.627
- Yeah.

00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:27.745
- It tastes like a rotten egg.

00:00:27.745 --> 00:00:29.240
- I actually kind of love it.

00:00:29.872 --> 00:00:31.434
- [Voiceover] Pickled green tomato.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:32.758
- Oh, it's not an olive, is it?

00:00:32.758 --> 00:00:34.192
- Wait, what is this?

00:00:34.432 --> 00:00:35.986
- Also smells like a pickle.

00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:38.974
- Ahh, I don't like this one.

00:00:38.974 --> 00:00:40.299
It just exploded.

00:00:40.299 --> 00:00:41.562
- It has the right amount of vinegar in it

00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:43.628
so it's not too sour.

00:00:43.628 --> 00:00:44.464
It's good.

00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:46.778
- I'd rather have 10 more eggs.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:48.229
- [Voiceover] A dilly bean?

00:00:48.229 --> 00:00:49.565
- Yeah, what does that even mean?

00:00:49.565 --> 00:00:50.609
- A green bean.

00:00:50.609 --> 00:00:51.306
- Cool.

00:00:51.306 --> 00:00:52.401
- Cheers.

00:00:52.401 --> 00:00:53.177
- No.

00:00:53.177 --> 00:00:54.791
- How could something be so rubbery

00:00:54.791 --> 00:00:56.578
and so crunchy at the same time?

00:00:56.578 --> 00:00:57.743
- It's like pickle's little cousin

00:00:57.743 --> 00:00:58.706
or something like that.

00:00:58.706 --> 00:00:59.798
Comes around sometimes.

00:00:59.798 --> 00:01:00.541
He's kinda cool.

00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:01.539
Not as cool as pickle,

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:02.514
but you tolerate him.

00:01:02.514 --> 00:01:03.068
Yeah.

00:01:03.068 --> 00:01:03.778
- [Voiceover] Pickled herring.

00:01:03.778 --> 00:01:04.578
- My first question is

00:01:04.578 --> 00:01:06.369
how long has this fish been dead?

00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:08.214
- I might be the only black person who

00:01:08.214 --> 00:01:10.413
grew up eating pickled
herring in the world.

00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:13.030
- Why?

00:01:14.045 --> 00:01:14.783
- No.

00:01:15.949 --> 00:01:17.781
- Oh yeah, you hate that.

00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:20.114
- It's soft. It's also rubbery.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.066
- My favorite thing so far.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.723
- Actually pickled watermelon?

00:01:23.723 --> 00:01:25.467
What part of the watermelon is this?

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.290
- It's the watermelon part.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.404
Oh, it's the what?

00:01:28.404 --> 00:01:29.066
- Yeah.

00:01:29.066 --> 00:01:30.633
- The skin of a watermelon?

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:32.574
- Why would you do that to a watermelon?

00:01:32.574 --> 00:01:34.263
- That has a slide to it.

00:01:36.403 --> 00:01:38.828
- This tastes like
something I've had before.

00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:40.950
- It's sweeter than you would think.
(coughing)

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.447
- That's so foul.

00:01:43.447 --> 00:01:44.405
- Tastes like a hotdog.

00:01:44.405 --> 00:01:45.499
(laughing)

00:01:45.499 --> 00:01:46.462
- Not bad.

00:01:46.462 --> 00:01:47.162
- Not bad at all.

00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:48.162
- It was like sweet.

00:01:48.162 --> 00:01:50.371
- [Voiceover] Actual pickles!

00:01:50.371 --> 00:01:51.847
- That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:51.927 --> 00:01:53.191
- That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:53.191 --> 00:01:53.993
- Cheers?

00:01:53.993 --> 00:01:54.683
- Cheers.

00:01:55.182 --> 00:01:56.262
- Oh yeah.

00:01:56.262 --> 00:01:57.342
Oh yeah. These are great.

00:01:57.342 --> 00:01:57.945
- Classic.

00:01:57.945 --> 00:01:59.849
It's a pickle, you don't
need to change anything.

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:00.881
Tastes great.

00:02:00.881 --> 00:02:02.940
- We should really just stick to

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.755
pickling cucumbers.

00:02:04.755 --> 00:02:06.143
(beat boxing)

00:02:07.158 --> 00:02:08.470
- ♫ I love pickles

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:09.735
♫ They are delicious

00:02:09.735 --> 00:02:12.576
♫ I also like sometimes canicious

00:02:12.576 --> 00:02:15.479
♫ I go to your house and
I don't do the dishes ♫

00:02:16.053 --> 00:02:17.019
That's all I got.

00:02:17.019 --> 00:02:18.021
(laughing)

